.TH WERKMEISTER-REGISTRY 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-registry \- Regenerate ~/.werkmeister/services.yaml from every \e<repo>/.werkmeister/services.yaml under paths.repos_root (merged under ~/.werkmeister/services.local.yaml)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister registry\fR [action]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Report drift without writing; nonzero exit when stale.
.TP
\fB\-\-from <worktree>\fR
Use this checkout's .werkmeister/services.yaml for its repo (needs \-\-out).
.TP
\fB\-\-out <file>\fR
Write the registry here instead of ~/.werkmeister/services.yaml.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Regenerates \fB~/.werkmeister/services.yaml\fR from every repo's \fB.werkmeister/services.yaml\fR fragment under \fBpaths.repos_root\fR, merged under \fB~/.werkmeister/services.local.yaml\fR. It is the same step \fBwerkmeister machine setup\fR runs, on its own: use it after cloning a new repo. \fBwerkmeister pr status\fR runs it too when a merged PR changes a fragment and the repo sets \fBsync_on_merge: auto\fR (Ship detection).
.PP
To prove a fragment change before it merges, \fB\-\-from <worktree>\fR takes that checkout's \fB.werkmeister/services.yaml\fR in place of its repo's fragment under \fBpaths.repos_root\fR, and \fB\-\-out <file>\fR writes the merged registry there instead of \fB~/.werkmeister/services.yaml\fR (which is never touched, nor is \fBservices.local.yaml\fR seeded). \fB\-\-check\fR compares against \fB\-\-out\fR the same way.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister registry            # regenerate (sync is the default action)
werkmeister registry \-\-check    # report drift; nonzero exit when stale
werkmeister registry \-\-from ./werkmeister \-\-out /tmp/services.yaml          # branch fragment, temp registry
werkmeister registry \-\-check \-\-from ./werkmeister \-\-out /tmp/services.yaml  # is that file current?
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
